Package: GeneCastR
Title: Introduction Time and Spread of Genetic Variants Under
        Wright-Fisher Dynamics
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Michael", "Whitehouse", email = "michael.whitehouse@imperial.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits a Wright-Fisher model with genic selection and recurrent
    gene flow to panels of allele-frequency surveys, with optional per-deme
    hierarchies over the growth advantage and the effective size, and reports
    projected frequencies, presence and exceedance probabilities, and
    posteriors over the introduction time and the founding time of the
    lineage that was detected. The latent allele count is held on a lattice, so the
    likelihood is evaluated exactly by a forward-backward pass with no
    particle approximation, and the introduction time is marginalised
    analytically.
